#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ot-src-refresh: carry main's tool fixes into each die's wave source tree (MERGE-QUEUE-1, COORD order 2026-11-14 21:2x).

Kit generation and plan binds read SRC/tools/die_plan (and SRC/physical/common_flow, SRC/rtl/{lib,common}) of each die's own
source tree (kit_wave.json dies.<die>.src on dies.<die>.gen_host, plus item_inputs.*.src), never the pinned rt/current tree.
Without this step a fix landed on main never reaches a new kit or bind.

  ot-src-refresh refresh --from OLD --to NEW [--apply]     the files main changed OLD..NEW (scope below), per tree:
        missing in the tree                       -> ADD (new file)
        tree copy == NEW                          -> SAME
        tree copy == OLD (or any earlier main version of the file) -> REPLACE with NEW
        tree copy is a local edit                 -> 3-way merge (git merge-file tree OLD NEW); clean -> MERGE, else CONFLICT (kept)
        a file that a process on the gen host has open or names in its command line -> BUSY (kept, retried on the next run)
  ot-src-refresh catchup --since DATE [--apply]            the same for every file main changed since DATE (base = the
        earlier main version the tree copy equals; a local edit without a known base is reported LOCAL and kept)
  ot-src-refresh daily [--apply]   (OWNER/COORD 11-15: the ONLY automatic mode; timer 06:00, never per merge, never mid-wave)
        one batch of every file main changed since the last good daily run (~/merge-queue/src-refresh-last.json, per die):
        1. gen host: the merged content is STAGED in SRC/.mq-stage/<stamp>/ (no tree changed) and smoke-tested through that
           overlay (every .py of tools/die_plan compiles, the gen entry modules import, every import of a staged file resolves);
           a failing smoke -> nothing swapped for that die;
        2. swap on the gen host, then the gen host's exact result goes to every dies.<die>.gen_hosts replica (the wave gens on any
           of them: 00:26 11-15 replicas lacking core_view_sha broke 32 gens); a replica copy that equals the gen host's old copy
           is replaced, a different one is 3-way merged (kept on conflict);
        3. the same smoke on every host; any failure -> the die is rolled back on ALL its hosts (backups below) and reported.
  ot-src-refresh put --die <die> <path>... [--apply]   a hand change: the GEN HOST's copy -> every gen_hosts replica (never reads
        main; reports each file's gen host copy vs main)
  ot-src-refresh put --die <die> --from-main <path>... [--apply]   main's version -> the gen host AND every replica
Every write: backup SRC/.mq-refresh-bak/<stamp>/<path> (cp -p), new content to a temp file in the same dir, then os.replace
(copy+mv: a running bash / Python keeps the old inode).  SRC/MQ_REFRESH.log gets one line per write.  Without --apply: report only.
Scope: tools/ (not tools/fleet, tools/autopilot: those run from rt/current) + physical/common_flow + rtl/lib + rtl/common; no tests.
Result TSV ~/merge-queue/src-refresh.tsv; BUSY rows in ~/merge-queue/src-refresh-pending.json are retried with main's newest content.
"""
